# Developer Environment — Base Context

This machine is managed with [chezmoi](https://chezmoi.io). The dotfiles source
lives at `~/.local/share/chezmoi`. Files there use attribute prefixes
(`dot_`, `private_`, `executable_`, `run_`, `symlink_`) that are **not** part of
the deployed filename. Check `chezmoi target-path <source-path>` before assuming
where something lands, and use `literal_` to escape a payload whose real name
starts with a reserved prefix.

## Shell and CLI

- Interactive shell is Zsh; write scripts for Bash.
- Common commands are replaced: `ls` → `eza`, `cat` → `bat --paging=never`,
  `cd` → `z` (zoxide), `lg` → `lazygit`. Prefer these when suggesting commands.
- `rg` (ripgrep), `fd`, `fzf`, `jq`, `delta`, and `gh` are available.

## Toolchains

- `mise` manages per-directory runtime versions via `mise.toml`, `.mise.toml`,
  or `.tool-versions`, backed by shims in `~/.local/share/mise/shims`. Respect a
  project's pinned versions instead of installing your own.
- Language servers on `PATH`: `vtsls` (JS/TS), `pyright-langserver` (Python),
  `gopls` (Go), `rust-analyzer` (Rust). Use the project's own typecheck or lint
  command for final verification.

## Project conventions

- Read the nearest `AGENTS.md` before doing project work.
- Durable multi-session artifacts belong under `./.local/` and nowhere else:
  - `./.local/CONTEXT.md` — domain language and architectural vocabulary
  - `./.local/adr/` — architecture decision records (`0001-*.md`)
  - `./.local/specs/`, `./.local/tickets/`, `./.local/handoffs/`
  - `./.local/reports/`, `./.local/prototypes/`, `./.local/triage/`
- Check `./.local/` for prior session state before starting. Create
  subdirectories lazily, only when writing an artifact.
- Timestamp filenames in UTC as `YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ`.
- Preserve the project's existing policy on whether `.local/` is committed.
- User-authored deliverables are not agent state; leave them where the user put
  them.

## Working rules

- Inspect surrounding code — conventions, imports, formatting — before editing.
  Match what is already there.
- Do not add explanatory comments unless asked.
- Run the project's lint and typecheck after changes (`npm run lint`,
  `npm run typecheck`, `pytest`, `cargo check`, and so on).
- **Never commit, amend, push, or open a pull request unless explicitly asked.**

## Session-scoped context

If the environment variable `AX_SESSION_CONTEXT` is set, read the file it points
at before doing anything else. It describes a sandbox and model-routing boundary
that applies to this session only. If the variable is unset, you are running the
agent directly and no such boundary exists — do not claim otherwise.
